cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ShorList, please cite it as below."
title: "ShorList: an open catalogue of cryptographic forms"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shorlist/shorlist"
abstract: >-
  The open catalogue of the cryptographic forms Shor's algorithm breaks, and the
  post-quantum ones that replace them. Each row is one form in which a public-key
  algorithm appears in source code or configuration, with a minimal context file, the
  expected detection and a primary source; decoy rows measure false alarms. A generator
  plants each row and scores a scanner's output against it, repeatably.
type: dataset
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Tenev
    given-names: Stanimir
    affiliation: Elkan Electronic
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - cryptographic inventory
  - CBOM
  - benchmark
  - static analysis
